$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. Procedure for the Synthesis of
2,3-Disubstituted Pyrazinium Salts 2,3-Diarylpyrazines were synthesized
from 2,3-dichloropyrazine with different aryl boronic acids through
Pd-catalyzed Suzuki coupling. Substrates S5iand S5jwere commecially
available. The substrates S5a, 4a S5b, 4b S5c, 4c S5d, 4d S5e 4c and S5h
4d were known compounds. Under nitrogen atmosphere, aryl boronic acid
(8.8 mmol) was added to a mixture of 2,3-dichloropyrazine (596 mg, 4.0
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (46 mg, 0.04 mmol), toluene (12.0 mL), and water (12.0
mL). The resulted solution was heated at 95 °C for 10 min. Then, it was
cooled down to room temperature. Then, potassium fluoride dihydrate (828
mg, 8.8 mmol) was added in one portion. The resulted mixture was stirred
and heated at 95 °C until the starting material was consumed. The mixture
was cooled down and the phases were separated. The aqueous phase was
extracted with ethyl acetate (10 mL×2). The combined organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated in vacuo.
Column chromatography of the residue on silica gel using petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate (5:1) as the eluent.
2,3-Bis(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)pyrazine (S5g): 1444 mg, white solid.
mp 129-130 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ8.67 (s, 2H), 7.67-7.53 (m, 8H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ151.5, 142.9, 141.6, 131.0 (q, JC-F = 32.4 Hz),
130.1, 125.5 (q, JC-F = 3.7 Hz), 123.9 (q, JC-F = 270.7 Hz); 19F NMR (376
MHz, CDCl3) δ-62.8. HRMS Calculated for C18H11F6N2[M+H]+ 369.0821, found
369.0821.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Chiral Piperazines via Hydrogenation of Pyrazines Activated
by Alkyl Halides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
