$DATUM To a stirred solution of phenylboronic acid (28.7 mg, 0.236 mmol),
1-(3-bromopyridin-4-yl)piperidine-4-carboxamide (67 mg, 0.24 mmol) and
Pd(dppf)Cl2 (5 mol%) in MeCN (1.6 mL) was added aqueous sodium carbonate
solution (0.5 M, 0.660 mL, 0.330 mmol). The reaction vessel was sealed
and heated in a focused microwave reactor to 120 ºC for 2 h, then for a
further 30 min at 150 ºC. The cooled reaction mixture was concentrated
under reduced pressure and the crude product was purified over a silica
cartridge (25 g) using a solvent system of 0-15% ethanol in
dichloromethane. The title compound 27 was isolated as a colourless solid
(65 mg, 98% yield). 1-(3-Phenylpyridin-4-yl)piperidine-4-carboxamide (27)
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.63-1.81 (m, 4H), 2.25 (tt, J = 11.4, 4.1 Hz,
1H), 2.68 (t, J = 12.1 Hz, 2H), 3.42 (br d, J = 12.1, 2H), 5.38 (s, 1H),
5.51 (s, 1H), 6.88 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H), 7.34-7.38 (m, 1H), 7.45 (t, J =
7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.49-7.53 (m, 2H), 8.23 (s, 1H), 8.32 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.2, 41.8, 49.3, 112.1, 122.7, 127.9, 128.0,
129.1, 137.6, 146.9, 149.2, 157.1, 176.4; LC (Method A) - MS (ESI, m/z)
Rt = 0.67 min – 282 (M+H)+ . ESI-HRMS: Found: 282.1601 calculated for
C17H20N3O (M+H)+: 282.1601.
